ion **WI-568**, which owns the keep/discard split and the last_approved REGENERATION (never copy the branch bytes). Flagged to WI-568: LLR-203/204 land Approved (branch's pre-OI-72 commit 580df781) vs OI-72's \"four Drafted rows\" reading."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":184104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":509},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a148e95e-cb6b-4656-8f3a-e7379c81b6de","uuid":"6233d39f-877d-4814-877b-194dd3122078","request_id":"req_011CedQ91CLv2Y9kjf1LGooF"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NhJTvq5L1W2eyZkS5no4vC","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a148e95e-cb6b-4656-8f3a-e7379c81b6de","uuid":"a3cf98f6-ca14-4d31-93f1-dde4b5d55508","timestamp":"2026-09-01T21:06:12.388Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons.md","oldString":"- **Refresh-conflict remedy** (generated files only, precedent 52faa5d8): merge trunk into the lane, REGENERATE the conflicted artifacts (gen_trajectory, derive_stage), commit, then re-note the rollup so it stays the newest commit — the verdict clock peels only the station's self-attested refresh commits.","newString":"- **Refresh-conflict remedy** (generated files only, precedent 52faa5d8): merge trunk into the lane, REGENERATE the conflicted artifacts (gen_trajectory, derive_stage), commit, then re-note the rollup so it stays the newest commit — the verdict clock peels only the station's self-attested refresh commits.\n- **The refresh trunk step regenerates the `[generated]` artifacts but NOT the approval brief `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md`** — so a lane that resolved a CURRENT.md merge conflict by taking trunk's side REDS the refresh bar's `approval-fresh` check until you run `trace.py --approve modified --out docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` on the branch and commit. Hit executing OI-71 (WI-555, 2026-09-01). The refresh is fail-closed: a red bar `reset --hard`s the branch and leaves trunk untouched, so measuring the merge is safe. A transient `git: Unable to write index` can abort the `--no-ff` step with trunk untouched — just retry once merge-ready.\n- **OI-71 done (WI-555, 2026-09-01)**: the held wi508 lane was converted complete→partial MANUALLY (create local ref at the origin HELD branch = \"rename back\"; `git mv` the spec archive/complete→active to undo the self-close; `handback.close_partial`; then `integrate.py integrate` from trunk root) and merged (trunk→551d1b2c). It minted disposition **WI-568**, which owns the keep/discard split and the last_approved REGENERATION (never copy the branch bytes). Flagged to WI-568: LLR-203/204 land Approved (branch's pre-OI-72 commit 580df781) vs OI-72's \"four Drafted rows\" reading.","originalFile":"---\nname: supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons\ndescription: \"2026-09-01 supervised-unpause lessons — integrate from trunk root only, the rollup-compile + drawn-round duties until WI-558/WI-559 land, and this Mac's box traps\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 57c88b47-5469-4e50-bc76-c5299aeea493\n  modified: 2026-09-01T12:18:43.669Z\n---\n\nFrom the 2026-09-01 supervised unpause (5 rows merged: WI-543/552/553/563/566; decisions 47–51):\n\n- **Until WI-558 lands**, every merge needs the supervisor to compile `docs/reviews/WI-<n>-REVIEW-A.md` on the lane from the round files (time-ordered, governing line last) — the verdict gate requires it and nothing writes it. **Until WI-559 lands**, adjudication lanes get NO review round yet their exit banner claims \"review round approved\" — draw a real round via an independent Opus subagent with a hostile brief (the drawn rounds caught real defects twice: a live --strict ERROR and a 17-row census inflation).\n- **Run `integrate.py` from the TRUNK root, never from inside a lane worktree** — the auto-unload deletes the script's own directory mid-run and post-merge intake crashes (`ModuleNotFoundError: intake`), leaving disposition drafts unminted. Recovery: call `intake.intake_after_merge` directly with the merge's own scope; `intake.py sweep` is structurally unusable (it sweeps ALL terminal folders and the OI-70 guard bites pre-convention rows like WI-457 — kit defect, decision 49).\n- **Refresh-conflict remedy** (generated files only, precedent 52faa5d8): merge trunk into the lane, REGENERATE the conflicted artifacts (gen_trajectory, derive_stage), commit, then re-note the rollup so it stays the newest commit — the verdict clock peels only the station's self-attested refresh commits.\n- **This Mac's traps**: bare `python` doesn't exist (use .venv or python3 — workers hit 127 three times); the lane pre-commit hook resolves ruff via SYSTEM python3 → loud format-SKIP on every worktree commit; never chain the loop launch into a compound foreground Bash (2-min timeout killed it mid-claim once — parked branch resumed fine).\n- The claim-refusal on status.md prose ids applies to ANY hand-authored mention including an embedded supervisor prompt (decision 47). OpenAI provider limit resets ~08:40 UTC; rounds before that run `-relaxed` (record them).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":5,"newStart":13,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Until WI-558 lands**, every merge needs the supervisor to compile `docs/reviews/WI-<n>-REVIEW-A.md` on the lane from the round files (time-ordered, governing line last) — the verdict gate requires it and nothing writes it. **Until WI-559 lands**, adjudication lanes get NO review round yet their exit banner claims \"review round approved\" — draw a real round via an independent Opus subagent with a hostile brief (the drawn rounds caught real defects twice: a live --strict ERROR and a 17-row census inflation)."," - **Run `integrate.py` from the TRUNK root, never from inside a lane worktree** — the auto-unload deletes the script's own directory mid-run and post-merge intake crashes (`ModuleNotFoundError: intake`), leaving disposition drafts unminted. Recovery: call `intake.intake_after_merge` directly with the merge's own scope; `intake.py sweep` is structurally unusable (it sweeps ALL terminal folders and the OI-70 guard bites pre-convention rows like WI-457 — kit defect, decision 49)."," - **Refresh-conflict remedy** (generated files only, precedent 52faa5d8): merge trunk into the lane, REGENERATE the conflicted artifacts (gen_trajectory, derive_stage), commit, then re-note the rollup so it stays the newest commit — the verdict clock peels only the station's self-attested refresh commits.","+- **The refresh trunk step regenerates the `[generated]` artifacts but NOT the approval brief `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md`** — so a lane that resolved a CURRENT.md merge conflict by taking trunk's side REDS the refresh bar's `approval-fresh` check until you run `trace.py --approve modified --out docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` on the branch and commit. Hit executing OI-71 (WI-555, 2026-09-01). The refresh is fail-closed: a red bar `reset --hard`s the branch and leaves trunk untouched, so measuring the merge is safe. A transient `git: Unable to write index` can abort the `--no-ff` step with trunk untouched — just retry once merge-ready.","+- **OI-71 done (WI-555, 2026-09-01)**: the held wi508 lane was converted complete→partial MANUALLY (create local ref at the origin HELD branch = \"rename back\"; `git mv` the spec archive/complete→active to undo the self-close; `handback.close_partial`; then `integrate.py integrate` from trunk root) and merged (trunk→551d1b2c). It minted disposition **WI-568**, which owns the keep/discard split and the last_approved REGENERATION (never copy the branch bytes). Flagged to WI-568: LLR-203/204 land Approved (branch's pre-OI-72 commit 580df781) vs OI-72's \"four Drafted rows\" reading."," - **This Mac's traps**: bare `python` doesn't exist (use .venv or python3 — workers hit 127 three times); the lane pre-commit hook resolves ruff via SYSTEM python3 → loud format-SKIP on every worktree commit; never chain the loop launch into a compound foreground Bash (2-min timeout killed it mid-claim once — parked branch resumed fine)."," - The claim-refusal on status.md prose ids applies to ANY hand-authored mention including an embedded supervisor prompt (decision 47). OpenAI provider limit resets ~08:40 UTC; rounds before that run `-relaxed` (record them)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
